IMPORT prelude

-- Communicable Diseases Agency Act 2025 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a person or business who meets the Agency: the
-- meaning of "infectious disease" (s 2), the offences of using the Agency's symbol (s 8) or its name or "CDA" (s 9), the secrecy
-- offence (s 35), protection from personal liability (s 36), compounding (s 44), the liability of a company's officers (s 45),
-- service of documents (s 47(5), (6)), and the transfer of Health Promotion Board and Ministry of Health staff (ss 49, 51 and the
-- Schedule); with the membership rules a would-be member meets (ss 10, 12(2), 19, 21(1)(g), 25).
--
-- Edition: the Act as enacted (No. 4 of 2025), informal consolidation, "version in force from 1/4/2025", as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/CDAA2025.txt (retrieved 1 October 2026, "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026"). The deposit shows no
-- amendment annotations. s 1 leaves commencement to a Gazette notification; that it commenced on 1 April 2025 is an INFERENCE from
-- the consolidation date, not something the text says.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0163 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The Act is almost wholly constitutional: it creates the Agency and gives it functions, but confers NO power over
-- the public. (INFERENCE, not read: the powers that touch a patient or a business are in the Infectious Diseases Act 1976; s 54(4)
-- only swaps "the Board" for the Agency in four of its provisions.) SCOPED accordingly. Not encoded: the functions and powers (ss 5, 6) beyond s
-- 5(4), ministerial directions (s 7), appointment mechanics (ss 11, 13-18, 20, 22), meetings beyond the quorum (ss 23, 24, 26-28),
-- committees and delegation (ss 29-32), the Chief Executive and officers (ss 33, 34), finance (ss 37-43), unincorporated
-- associations (s 46, which mirrors s 45), regulations (s 48), the transfer of assets and records (ss 50, 53), employment
-- continuity beyond the transfer itself (s 52), and the consequential amendments and savings (ss 54, 55).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the naive rows (writing-l4-rules not loadable). No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Communicable Diseases Agency Act 2025`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS IF `a` LESS THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the higher of` MEANS IF `a` GREATER THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `2 -- infectious disease`

-- s 2: "infectious disease" means any disease "(a) that is caused or is suspected to be caused by a micro-organism or any agent of
-- disease; and (b) that is capable or is suspected to be capable of transmission by any means to human beings". Both limbs, and
-- suspicion is enough for each.
GIVEN `caused or suspected to be caused by a micro-organism or agent of disease` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `capable or suspected capable of transmission to humans` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an infectious disease` IF
    `caused or suspected to be caused by a micro-organism or agent of disease` AND `capable or suspected capable of transmission to humans`

§§ `8 -- the Agency's symbol`

-- s 8(1): the Agency has "the exclusive right to the use of" its symbols or representations. (2) A person who "(a) uses, without the
-- prior written permission of the Agency, a symbol or representation identical to" the Agency's; or "(b) uses a symbol or
-- representation that so resembles" it "as to deceive or cause confusion, or to be likely to deceive or to cause confusion" is guilty
-- of an offence: "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or ... both".
-- On the words, the permission defence is written into limb (a) only; limb (b) has none. That is a literal reading.
GIVEN `uses an identical symbol` IS A BOOLEAN, `uses a confusingly similar symbol` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `had the Agency's prior written permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using the symbol is an offence` IF
        (`uses an identical symbol` AND (NOT `had the Agency's prior written permission`))
    OR  `uses a confusingly similar symbol`

§§ `9 -- the name and the acronym CDA`

-- s 9(1): the Agency "may conduct its operations under its full name or under the acronym CDA". (2) "A person other than the Agency
-- must not -- (a) use in connection with a business, trade, profession or occupation; (b) use as the name, or as part of the name, of
-- any firm, body corporate or institution; or (c) use in relation to -- (i) services or products; or (ii) the promotion ... of the
-- supply of services or products, the name of the Agency or the acronym CDA, or a name or acronym so closely resembling [them] as to
-- be likely to be mistaken for it." (3) $10,000 or 6 months or both. There is no permission exception in s 9.
DECLARE NameUse IS ONE OF
    `in connection with a business, trade, profession or occupation`
    `as the name or part of the name of a firm, company or institution`
    `in relation to services or products or their promotion`
    `in a news report about the Agency`
    `in private conversation`

GIVEN `the user is the Agency` IS A BOOLEAN, `the name or CDA or a name likely to be mistaken for it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the use` IS A NameUse
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using the name is an offence` IF
        (NOT `the user is the Agency`)
    AND `the name or CDA or a name likely to be mistaken for it`
    AND CONSIDER `the use`
        WHEN `in a news report about the Agency` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `in private conversation` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `8, 9, 35 and 44 -- penalties and compounding`

-- Penalties: s 8(2) and s 9(3) "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or ... both";
-- s 35(2) "a fine not exceeding $2,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or ... both". The secrecy offence
-- has the lower fine but the longer prison term.
-- s 44(1): the Chief Executive or an authorised employee "may compound any offence under this Act that is prescribed as a
-- compoundable offence by collecting ... a sum not exceeding the lower of the following: (a) one half of the amount of the maximum
-- fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $2,000." (2) no further proceedings on payment; (3) sums go to the Consolidated
-- Fund. Which offences are prescribed was not retrieved: "prescribed as compoundable" is an input.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `misusing the Agency's symbol`
    `misusing the Agency's name or CDA`
    `disclosing Agency information`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `disclosing Agency information` THEN 2000
    OTHERWISE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `disclosing Agency information` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 6

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that may be collected to compound` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`the maximum fine` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 2000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `sum collected` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the composition is within section 44` IF
    `prescribed as compoundable` AND `sum collected` AT MOST `the most that may be collected to compound` `the offence`

§§ `35 -- preservation of secrecy`

-- s 35(1): "A member, an officer, an agent or a delegate of the Agency, the Chief Executive or a committee member, who has
-- information in his or her capacity as such that would not otherwise be available to him or her, must not disclose that
-- information to any person except -- (a) in the performance of the Agency's functions; (b) with the prior authorisation from the
-- Agency to do so; (c) for the purposes of any proceedings for an offence under this Act, or any report of those proceedings;
-- (d) as required by an order of court; (e) in complying with the requirements in this Act ... to disclose an interest; or (f) as
-- required or allowed by this Act or any other Act." s 2: "officer" includes a secondee.
DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `performing the Agency's functions`
    `with the Agency's prior authorisation`
    `proceedings for an offence under this Act`
    `an order of court`
    `disclosing an interest as this Act requires`
    `as required or allowed by an Act`
    `telling a journalist`
    `telling a friend`

DECLARE Disclosure HAS
    `made by a member, officer, agent, delegate, Chief Executive or committee member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `information held in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `information otherwise available to the discloser` IS A BOOLEAN
    `purpose` IS A Purpose

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purpose is an exception in section 35(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `telling a journalist` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `telling a friend` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is an offence under section 35` IF
        `the disclosure`'s `made by a member, officer, agent, delegate, Chief Executive or committee member`
    AND `the disclosure`'s `information held in that capacity`
    AND (NOT `the disclosure`'s `information otherwise available to the discloser`)
    AND (NOT `the purpose is an exception in section 35(1)` (`the disclosure`'s `purpose`))

§§ `36 -- protection from personal liability`

-- s 36: "No liability shall lie against any member of the Agency, any committee member, the Chief Executive or any officer or
-- delegate of the Agency, or any other person acting under the direction of the Agency, for anything which is done or purported to
-- be done, or omitted to be done, in good faith and with reasonable care in -- (a) the performance or purported performance of any
-- function under this Act; or (b) the exercise or purported exercise of any power under this Act." Good faith AND reasonable care:
-- good faith alone does not protect a careless act. Note "under this Act": acts under the Infectious Diseases Act 1976 are not
-- covered by this section (whether that Act protects them was not read).
GIVEN `a member, officer, delegate or person acting under the Agency's direction` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `with reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in performing a function or exercising a power under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is protected by section 36` IF
        `a member, officer, delegate or person acting under the Agency's direction`
    AND `in good faith`
    AND `with reasonable care`
    AND `in performing a function or exercising a power under this Act`

§§ `45 -- officers of a corporation`

-- s 45(2): where a corporation commits an offence under this Act, a person "(a) who is -- (i) an officer of the corporation; or (ii)
-- an individual involved in the management of the corporation and in a position to influence the conduct of the corporation in
-- relation to the commission of the offence; and (b) who -- (i) consented or connived, or conspired with others, to effect the
-- commission of the offence; (ii) is ... knowingly concerned in, or is party to, the commission of the offence ...; or (iii) knew or
-- ought reasonably to have known that the offence ... would be or is being committed, and failed to take all reasonable steps to
-- prevent or stop the commission of that offence, shall be guilty of that same offence". (5) This applies "whether or not the
-- corporation is convicted". (6) "corporation" includes a limited liability partnership.
DECLARE Individual HAS
    `an officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in management and able to influence the conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consented, connived or conspired` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knowingly concerned or party to it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew or ought reasonably to have known` IS A BOOLEAN
    `took all reasonable steps to prevent or stop it` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the corporation committed an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `the individual` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual is guilty of the same offence` IF
        `the corporation committed an offence under this Act`
    AND (`the individual`'s `an officer of the corporation` OR `the individual`'s `in management and able to influence the conduct`)
    AND (    `the individual`'s `consented, connived or conspired`
         OR  `the individual`'s `knowingly concerned or party to it`
         OR  (`the individual`'s `knew or ought reasonably to have known` AND (NOT `the individual`'s `took all reasonable steps to prevent or stop it`)))

§§ `47(5), (6) -- when service takes effect`

-- s 47(5): service takes effect "(a) if the document is sent by fax and a notification of successful transmission is received, on
-- the day of transmission; (b) if the document is sent by email, at the time that the email becomes capable of being retrieved ...;
-- or (c) if the document is sent by prepaid registered post, 2 days after the day the document was posted (even if it is returned
-- undelivered)." (6) "service of any document under this Act on a person by email may be effected only with the person's prior
-- written consent to service in that way." (7) Not for court documents. Days are counted as day numbers.
GIVEN `day posted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day registered-post service takes effect` MEANS `day posted` PLUS 2

GIVEN `the person gave prior written consent to email service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `service by email is permitted` IF `the person gave prior written consent to email service`

§§ `49, 51 and the Schedule -- who moved to the Agency`

-- s 51(1): on the transfer date every "transferring HPB employee" and "transferring MOH employee" stops being an employee of the
-- Health Promotion Board or the Government and "becomes an employee, of the Agency on terms no less favourable than those enjoyed by
-- the employee on the eve of the transfer date". s 49: the transferring employees are those, on the eve of the transfer date, in the
-- departments in the Schedule: Part 1 (HPB) "Preventive Health Programs & Rewards Division, Communicable Diseases Branch" and
-- "Research, Evaluation and Monitoring Division, National Immunisation Registry Branch"; Part 2 (MOH) "Communicable Diseases Policy
-- and Preparedness Division", "Surveillance, Epidemiology and Response Division" and "the Interim Communicable Diseases Agency".
-- s 51(3): the transfer "(a) does not interrupt continuity ...; (b) does not constitute a retrenchment or redundancy ...; and (c) does
-- not entitle that employee to any compensation". (5) s 18A of the Employment Act 1968 does not apply. The two non-Schedule
-- departments below are illustrative.
DECLARE Department IS ONE OF
    `HPB Communicable Diseases Branch`
    `HPB National Immunisation Registry Branch`
    `MOH Communicable Diseases Policy and Preparedness Division`
    `MOH Surveillance, Epidemiology and Response Division`
    `MOH Interim Communicable Diseases Agency`
    `another HPB department`
    `another MOH division`

GIVEN `the department` IS A Department
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the department is in the Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `the department`
    WHEN `another HPB department` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `another MOH division` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `an employee on the eve of the transfer date` IS A BOOLEAN, `the department` IS A Department
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee transferred to the Agency` IF
    `an employee on the eve of the transfer date` AND `the department is in the Schedule` `the department`

-- s 51(1)(b): "on terms no less favourable than those enjoyed by the employee on the eve of the transfer date". The text compares
-- terms as a whole; this encoding compares monthly salary only, as a stand-in (an encoding simplification, not the text).
-- s 51(4)(a): terms may be altered "by or under any law, award or agreement with effect from any time after the transfer date", so
-- the comparison is of the terms on transfer only.
GIVEN `salary on the eve of the transfer date` IS A NUMBER, `salary with the Agency on transfer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer terms are no less favourable` IF
    `salary with the Agency on transfer` AT LEAST `salary on the eve of the transfer date`

§§ `10, 12(2), 19, 21(1)(g) and 25 -- who may sit on the Agency`

-- s 10(1): "The Agency consists of at least 7 and not more than 15 members."
GIVEN `number of members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the membership size is lawful` IF
    `number of members` AT LEAST 7 AND `number of members` AT MOST 15

-- s 12(2): disqualified are "(a) an undischarged bankrupt or an individual who has an arrangement with any of his or her
-- creditors; (b) a Judge or judicial officer; (c) an individual who has been sentenced to imprisonment for a term of 6 months or
-- more, and has not received a free pardon; (d) [a director disqualified under the Companies Act 1967 or the Variable Capital
-- Companies Act 2018, during the disqualification]; (e) an individual who lacks capacity ... within the meaning of the Mental
-- Capacity Act 2008, or [subject to] an order ... under section 10 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) Act 2008." A conviction
-- with a fine only, or a sentence under 6 months, does not disqualify.
DECLARE Candidate HAS
    `an undischarged bankrupt or in an arrangement with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a Judge or judicial officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months of imprisonment sentenced` IS A NUMBER
    `received a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN
    `currently disqualified as a company or VCC director` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lacks capacity or under a mental health order` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the candidate` IS A Candidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate is disqualified` IF
        `the candidate`'s `an undischarged bankrupt or in an arrangement with creditors`
    OR  `the candidate`'s `a Judge or judicial officer`
    OR  (`the candidate`'s `months of imprisonment sentenced` AT LEAST 6 AND (NOT `the candidate`'s `received a free pardon`))
    OR  `the candidate`'s `currently disqualified as a company or VCC director`
    OR  `the candidate`'s `lacks capacity or under a mental health order`

-- s 19(1): "each member of the Agency holds office for a period of 3 years or any shorter period specified in the instrument of
-- appointment." (2) "A member of the Agency may be re-appointed." No limit on re-appointment is stated.
GIVEN `years in the instrument` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the term is within section 19` IF `years in the instrument` AT MOST 3

-- s 21(1)(g): a member ceases to hold office if he or she "fails to attend 3 consecutive meetings of the Agency without the approval
-- of the Agency". (2) No compensation for ceasing to hold office "for any reason".
GIVEN `consecutive meetings missed` IS A NUMBER, `with the Agency's approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member ceases to hold office for absence` IF
    `consecutive meetings missed` AT LEAST 3 AND (NOT `with the Agency's approval`)

-- s 25(1): "The quorum for a meeting of the Agency is the higher of the following: (a) one-third of the number of members; (b) 3
-- members." (2) "No business may be transacted at a meeting of the Agency if a quorum is not present." One-third may be a fraction;
-- quorate is tested by comparing three times those present with the membership, not by rounding.
GIVEN `number of members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the quorum` MEANS `the higher of` (`number of members` DIVIDED BY 3) 3

GIVEN `present` IS A NUMBER, `number of members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `business may be transacted` IF
    `present` TIMES 3 AT LEAST `number of members` AND `present` AT LEAST 3
